  "summary": "A recap of the 2026 Washington legislative session highlights passage of SB 6002, which regulates automated license plate readers and generally requires data deletion within three weeks, alongside a millionaires' income tax and other measures. The article notes ALPR concerns including misuse by stalkers and sharing with federal immigration enforcement, and mentions Olympia and Everett among jurisdictions that considered suspending ALPR programs.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Senate Bill 6002 by Sen. Yasmin Trudeau, a Tacoma Democrat, creates regulations for using ALPR systems and limits their use by local and state agencies. Data generally must be deleted within three weeks, with certain exceptions.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "the law now is that the data stays in Washington for the purposes of solving serious crimes that are listed in the bill",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
